---- ENDF/B-VIII.1    MATERIAL    3         REVISION 1               3 1451
----- THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                                3 1451
------ ENDF-6                                                        3 1451
                                                                     3 1451
******************************************************************   3 1451
                                                                     3 1451
This evaluation is based on the methodology presented in [1].        3 1451
Path-integral molecular dynamics techniques have been used           3 1451
to produce the input for the neutron scattering model at the         3 1451
indicated temperatures. This includes the radial distribution and    3 1451
velocity autocorrelation functions, which were used to generate      3 1451
the static structure factor and the frequency spectrum. The static   3 1451
structure factor has been used to compute the coherent scattering    3 1451
function with the Skold approximation. For the dynamics, the         3 1451
frequency spectrum was decomposed into solid-like and diffusive      3 1451
parts, which were convoluted with vibrational and rotaional          3 1451
components using previously existing methods [2,3]. This formalism   3 1451
is coded in NJOY-H2D2 [4], which was used to generate the library.   3 1451
                                                                     3 1451
The approach has been benchmarked against previously existing        3 1451
libraries, theoretical calculations and available experimental       3 1451
data in [1].                                                         3 1451
                                                                     3 1451
